  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Calm weather conditions expected to \ncontinue over the next several days with unseasonably warm \ntemperatures today and Friday, as highs reach several degrees above \nnormal. Over the weekend, a low pressure system will move into the \nnorthwestern CONUS, which will tighten surface pressure gradients, \nincreasing winds Saturday. Winds on Saturday are  expected to be up \nto 20-25 mph sustained and gusts up to 45 mph. A Fire Weather Watch \nremains in effect for all zones Saturday as minimum relative \nhumidity values will drop to as low as 9 percent Saturday afternoon. \nThe low pressure system will also drag much cooler air into Nevada \nwith highs reaching to near normal Saturday, then dropping to \nseveral degrees below normal Sunday. Into the next week, \ntemperatures will slightly warm but expected to stay around normal \nwith light winds.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence regarding \nunseasonably warm temperatures today and Friday. Moderate confidence \nin strong, gusty winds and cooler temperatures over the weekend. No \nchanges to NBM grids at this time.",
